# Agent actions

- Declare agent capabilities in `plugin/django/<app>/actions.py` with `domain()` and `@action`,
  listed in `PLUGIN.actions`; never write a `tools.py`, a `BaseTool` subclass or a `@tool`
  function. Skill: `yeshuman-agent-actions`.
- Domain nouns come from the app's models (`NOUNS`) or ontology nouns, never screen labels or
  scope words (`lexicon`, `system`, `admin`, `manage`, `identity`, …). A pack never redeclares a
  core noun.
- Every action declares `kind` (READ / WRITE / DESTRUCTIVE / UI), a typed input and a typed result,
  and returns `ActionResult` with `entities` for what it changed.
- Inputs never carry the acting context (`user_id`, `thread_id`, `focus`, `current_route`,
  `organisation_slug`, …): use `ctx`.
- Prompts, facts hints and config reference capabilities as `domain.action`, never a rendered
  tool name.
- Run the pack tests (`check_actions` in `plugin/django/tests/test_agent_actions.py`, and
  `plugin/django/tests/test_terminology.py`) before committing.
